    <!-- Does WIB Use DST? -->
    <section class="content-section" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2>Does WIB Observe Daylight Saving Time?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>No. Western Indonesia Time (WIB) does not observe daylight saving time.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        Because Indonesia is situated along the equator, daylight hours remain virtually uniform (roughly 12 hours of sunlight) throughout the entire year. Seasonal clock adjustments offer no daylight-saving benefit near the equator. Consequently, WIB remains fixed at UTC+7 year-round.
      </p>
      <p>
        This means the mathematical conversion formula is permanent: <strong>GMT + 7 hours = WIB</strong>, 365 days a year.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Date Changes -->
    <section class="content-section" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2>GMT to WIB Date Changes</h2>
      <p>
        Because WIB is 7 hours ahead of GMT, late afternoon and evening GMT times pass midnight and fall on the following calendar day in WIB.
      </p>
      <h3>Date Rollover Window</h3>
      <ul style="padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.9;">
        <li><strong>GMT 00:00 to 16:59</strong> → WIB 07:00 to 23:59 → <strong>Same calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>GMT 17:00</strong> → WIB 00:00 (midnight) → <strong>Next calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>GMT 18:00</strong> → WIB 01:00 AM → <strong>Next calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>GMT 21:00</strong> → WIB 04:00 AM → <strong>Next calendar day</strong></li>
        <li><strong>GMT 23:00</strong> → WIB 06:00 AM → <strong>Next calendar day</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Examples of Date Transition</h3>
      <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; margin: 1rem 0;">
        <p style="margin: 0 0 0.75rem;"><strong>Example 1:</strong> 4:00 PM GMT on August 10 → 11:00 PM WIB on August 10 (same day)</p>
        <p style="margin: 0 0 0.75rem;"><strong>Example 2:</strong> 5:00 PM GMT on August 10 → 12:00 AM WIB on August 11 (date advances)</p>
        <p style="margin: 0;"><strong>Example 3:</strong> 10:00 PM GMT on December 31 → 5:00 AM WIB on January 1 (new year in WIB!)</p>
      </div>
      <p>
        Always check both the <strong>time and date</strong> when scheduling across GMT and WIB. Our converter tool handles date transitions automatically.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Business & Scheduling -->
