      <h2>GMT to WIB for Meetings and Business</h2>
      <p>
        Coordinating business operations between Europe/GMT and Western Indonesia requires planning around the 7-hour time difference.
      </p>
      <h3>Overlapping Working Hours</h3>
      <p>
        Standard business hours in Jakarta (8:00 AM to 5:00 PM WIB) correspond to <strong>1:00 AM to 10:00 AM GMT</strong>. The most practical overlap window for real-time collaboration occurs between <strong>7:00 AM and 10:00 AM GMT (2:00 PM to 5:00 PM WIB)</strong>, offering a 3-hour daily window when both parties are in their offices.
      </p>
      <h3>Best Practices for International Scheduling</h3>
      <ul style="padding-left: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.9;">
        <li>Always state timezone abbreviations clearly: <strong>09:00 GMT / 16:00 WIB</strong></li>
        <li>Note that during European summer months (late March to late October), the UK operates on BST (UTC+1), which reduces the UK-to-WIB offset to 6 hours</li>
        <li>When scheduling morning calls from Europe, aim for 7:00–9:00 AM GMT to catch Indonesian colleagues before they leave work</li>
        <li>For digital events, webinars, or global product launches, 12:00 PM GMT maps to 7:00 PM WIB — ideal evening viewing in Jakarta</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

