      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem;">
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing WIB with WITA or WIT</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">Indonesia has 3 time zones. WIB is UTC+7 (Jakarta), WITA is UTC+8 (Bali), and WIT is UTC+9 (Papua). Using WIB for Bali creates a 1-hour error.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Forgetting the Date Rollover</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">GMT times from 5:00 PM onward roll into the next day in WIB. 6:00 PM GMT on Tuesday is 1:00 AM WIB on Wednesday.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Confusing GMT with BST</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">During summer, London uses BST (UTC+1), which is 6 hours behind WIB. Standard GMT (UTC+0) is always 7 hours behind WIB.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem;">
          <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem;">❌ Assuming Seasonal Clock Shifts</h3>
          <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.93rem;">WIB stays at UTC+7 year-round. Do not add or subtract hours for daylight saving in Indonesia.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

